prompt:
Review the scheduled-transfer pull request in this Node.js wallet ledger project. The worker is about to be enabled for recurring customer movements, so I need confidence that it fits the ledger rules and the surrounding operational behavior rather than only passing its new examples. Read the project files, the PR description at pr/5120/description.md, and the exact diff at pr/5120/changes.diff; use the existing docs and tests to understand the contracts. Write the review to REVIEW.md at the top of the project. Keep the prose focused on concrete consequences in this service and fixes a developer can apply. End the review with a fenced json list of findings, each with location (path/to/file.ext:LINE, using line numbers from the project as it is now), severity (critical, high, medium, low or nit), issue and fix.

```json
[
  {"location": "path/to/file.ext:LINE", "severity": "medium", "issue": "what is wrong and why it matters", "fix": "an actionable change"}
]
```
